string syncPurchaseInflow(string dryRun)
{
	// PURCHASED MATERIAL ARRIVING IN ZOHO INVENTORY, LANDED IN CREATOR.
	//
	// Purchase happens entirely in Inventory. This is the one thing that tells
	// Creator about it:
	//
	//   fabric      -> Raw_Material.Unallocated_Qty
	//   everything  -> Raw_Material.Quantity
	//   else
	//
	// Fabric goes to Unallocated_Qty and NOT into a lot, because a lot is a tone
	// and nobody has looked at the cloth yet. The store person drains it from the
	// "Unallocated quantity" tab, which is what assigns the tone. saveStockInward
	// already takes its quantity out of Unallocated_Qty before raising the parent
	// total, so that half needs no change at all - this function is only the
	// feeder the seam was built for.
	//
	// dryRun "true" computes every figure and writes NOTHING - not a ledger row,
	// not a quantity. Run it that way first; it is the only way to see what a
	// first run would do before it has done it.
	//
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// WHY A LEDGER FORM AND NOT A last-synced TIMESTAMP.
	//
	// Inventory_Inflow holds one row per (document, line), with what the document
	// says now and what Creator has taken in. Everything difficult falls out of
	// that one shape:
	//
	//   - APPLIED EXACTLY ONCE. The row is the record that it landed. No window,
	//     no clock skew, no "did the last run finish".
	//   - AN EDITED RECEIVE IS A DELTA. 200 corrected to 180 applies -20, because
	//     the row remembers the 200. Posting the total instead would add 180 on
	//     top of 200. Same rule as the finished-goods post in the build plan, for
	//     the same reason.
	//   - A DELETED LINE REVERSES. It is a key the ledger has and the document no
	//     longer does.
	//   - PROVENANCE. "Where did these 200 metres come from" is answerable, which
	//     it is not once a number has been added to a field.
	//
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// WHY NOT JUST COMPARE TOTALS. reconcileRawMaterial already reads
	// stock_on_hand per SKU and knows the difference against Creator. Turning it
	// into a writer would be a dozen lines and it is the WORST thing that could
	// be built here.
	//
	// Consumption posting is switched off today - receiveMaterials no longer
	// enqueues one. So every supervisor receipt lowers Creator and leaves
	// Inventory untouched, and a balance-driven sync would read that growing gap
	// as material that had arrived and credit it to Unallocated_Qty. Cloth that
	// was cut last week would come back as new stock, silently, for ever.
	//
	// So: DOCUMENT DRIVEN. Only an actual purchase document moves anything, and
	// only the part of it Creator has not already taken.
	//
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// THE CUTOVER DATE IS NOT OPTIONAL. Creator's opening balances were seeded
	// from Creator's own figures, and Inventory already holds purchase documents
	// from before this function existed. Without a floor, the first run would
	// read every one of them as an arrival and add stock that has been on the
	// rack for months. Nothing dated before cutoverDate is ever opened, so it
	// costs no call either - the floor is applied to the LIST, not to the line.
	//
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// CALL COST. A run is ONE list call in the steady state. A document is only
	// opened up line by line when the ledger has never seen it, or when its
	// last_modified_time has moved since - so an unchanged history costs nothing
	// however long it gets. maxDetail bounds a bad day; the rest waits for the
	// next run rather than risking the statement limit, which is not catchable
	// and shows as a bare 500 with no error card.

	res = "";
	errTxt = "";

	try
	{
		orgId = "60076905558";
		baseUrl = "https://www.zohoapis.in/inventory/v1/";

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// EVERY LOCATION COUNTS, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT.
		//
		// This was written to accept Main Warehouse only, on the reasoning that
		// a receive into Production is not cloth at the store counter. The first
		// real purchase receive on this org landed at HEAD OFFICE
		// (3955559000000032097), so that filter would have silently dropped a
		// genuine arrival - the worst shape this can fail in, because a skipped
		// arrival looks exactly like no arrival.
		//
		// The deeper reason is the reconciliation identity. reconcileRawMaterial
		// compares Creator against item.stock_on_hand, which is the ORG-WIDE
		// total across every location - Creator has no location concept anywhere
		// in it. So cloth received at any location is inside the number Creator
		// is measured against, and ignoring some locations guarantees permanent
		// drift that nothing can explain.
		//
		// A purchase receive only ever exists against a purchase order, so it is
		// always newly bought stock whatever door it came through. Where it
		// landed is recorded on the ledger row instead of being acted on, so if
		// this turns out to need the distinction the data is already there.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// WHICH DOCUMENT IS THE ARRIVAL. Zoho raises stock on ONE of the two,
		// never both: a purchase receive if receives are switched on, otherwise
		// the bill. Reading both double-counts every arrival.
		//
		// SET FROM probePurchaseInflow's verdict, once, and left alone. It is a
		// constant on purpose - auto-detecting per run would let the mode flip
		// underneath live data, which is the same silent corruption one level up.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		inflowSource = "Bill";

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// SET THIS TO THE DAY THE SYNC GOES LIVE, BEFORE THE FIRST REAL RUN.
		//
		// Nothing dated before it is ever looked at. Every purchase document
		// already in Inventory describes stock that is ALREADY inside Creator's
		// opening balances, so a floor that is too early adds months of history
		// to the rack a second time - and the first symptom is a store person
		// holding an Unallocated figure with no cloth behind it.
		//
		// Too late is the harmless direction: an arrival is simply not seen, the
		// store person says so, the date moves back.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		cutoverDate = '25-Aug-2026';

		// How far back the ledger is read and documents are considered. A
		// document older than this that is edited will be missed;
		// reconcileRawMaterial is the backstop that reports the gap.
		windowDays = 60;

		// Documents opened up line by line in one run.
		maxDetail = 12;

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// CREATING A Raw_Material FOR A PURCHASED ITEM CREATOR DOES NOT KNOW.
		//
		// Set autoCreate to false to go back to only reporting Unmapped rows.
		//
		// THE customfield_id VALUES COME FROM probeItemCustomFields AND MUST BE
		// MATCHED BY ID, NEVER BY LABEL. Custom fields come back only inside a
		// custom_fields array of {customfield_id, label, value} - there are no
		// cf_ keys - so matching on the label means renaming the field in
		// Inventory silently unclassifies every item, and the first symptom is
		// purchases quietly no longer landing. Settled as A3 in
		// inventory-integration.md.
		//
		// While cfProductType is empty nothing is ever created: an item that
		// cannot be classified is refused and says why, rather than being
		// guessed at. Only Product Type is load-bearing - the rest are
		// descriptive and an empty id simply leaves that column blank.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		autoCreate = true;
		cfProductType = "";
		cfTypeField = "";
		cfFabricWidth = "";
		cfGsmField = "";
		cfQualityField = "";
		cfPatternField = "";
		cfColorField = "";

		writeAllowed = true;
		drTxt = ifnull(dryRun,"").toString().trim().toLowerCase();
		if(drTxt == "true" || drTxt == "yes" || drTxt == "1")
		{
			writeAllowed = false;
			dryTxtOut = "true";
		}

		cutoffDate = zoho.currentdate.subDay(windowDays);
		if(cutoffDate < cutoverDate)
		{
			cutoffDate = cutoverDate;
		}

		listedCount = 0;
		detailCount = 0;
		appliedLines = 0;
		reversedLines = 0;
		unchangedDocs = 0;
		skippedDocs = 0;
		skippedLines = 0;
		deferredDocs = 0;
		unmappedLines = 0;
		blockedLines = 0;
		createdMats = 0;
		mappedNow = 0;
		widthMissing = 0;
		notRawLines = 0;

		// Emitted into the response rather than concatenated as a boolean -
		// building the JSON by hand means every value has to be a string this
		// function chose.
		dryTxtOut = "false";

		callsUsed = 0;
		netFabric = 0.0;
		netOther = 0.0;
		rowsJson = "";
		noteJson = "";
		listNote = "";

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// The map every arriving line has to resolve through. Keyed on the
		// Inventory id as TEXT - these are 18-digit values and a mixed-type
		// comparison throws.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		matByInv = Map();
		skuByInv = Map();
		fabByInv = Map();

		// Materials that already exist under a SKU but carry no
		// Inventory_Item_ID - the mapInventoryItemIds leftovers. Built in the
		// same pass rather than scanned per unknown item, which would be a full
		// walk of Raw_Material inside the line loop.
		//
		// Keyed UPPER-CASED and trimmed, the same way lot numbers are compared,
		// so RM-00011 cannot slip in beside rm-00011 and mint a duplicate.
		unmappedIdBySku = Map();
		unmappedFabBySku = Map();

		for each  rmRow in Raw_Material[ID != 0]
		{
			rmInv = ifnull(rmRow.Inventory_Item_ID,"").toString().trim();
			rmSkuTxt = ifnull(rmRow.SKU,"").toString().trim();

			if(rmInv == "" && rmSkuTxt != "")
			{
				rmSkuUp = rmSkuTxt.toUpperCase();

				if(unmappedIdBySku.get(rmSkuUp) == null)
				{
					rmFabU = ifnull(rmRow.Is_Fabric,"").toString().trim().toLowerCase();
					unmappedIdBySku.put(rmSkuUp,rmRow.ID + "");

					if(rmFabU == "true" || rmFabU == "yes" || rmFabU == "1" || rmFabU == "y")
					{
						unmappedFabBySku.put(rmSkuUp,"yes");
					}
					else
					{
						unmappedFabBySku.put(rmSkuUp,"no");
					}
				}
			}

			if(rmInv != "")
			{
				matByInv.put(rmInv,rmRow.ID + "");
				skuByInv.put(rmInv,ifnull(rmRow.SKU,"").toString().trim());

				// As TEXT, never against the boolean true. A Decision box gives a
				// boolean, a yes/no dropdown gives the string "Yes", an untouched
				// field gives EMPTY - and only the first matches == true. Reading
				// it wrong sends fabric into Quantity, where the lots can never
				// find it and no screen in the app reads it.
				rmFab = ifnull(rmRow.Is_Fabric,"").toString().trim().toLowerCase();

				if(rmFab == "true" || rmFab == "yes" || rmFab == "1" || rmFab == "y")
				{
					fabByInv.put(rmInv,"yes");
				}
				else
				{
					fabByInv.put(rmInv,"no");
				}
			}
		}

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// The ledger, bounded by the same window. Three indexes off one scan:
		// what each line has already taken in, which Creator row holds it, and
		// which version of each document was last read.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		appliedByKey = Map();
		rowIdByKey = Map();
		modByDoc = Map();
		keysByDoc = Map();
		retryDocs = List();

		for each  lgRow in Inventory_Inflow[Doc_Date >= cutoffDate]
		{
			lgDoc = ifnull(lgRow.Doc_ID,"").toString().trim();
			lgLine = ifnull(lgRow.Line_ID,"").toString().trim();

			if(lgDoc != "")
			{
				lgKey = lgDoc + "|" + lgLine;

				//----------------------------------------------------------
				// A DOCUMENT HOLDING UNFINISHED WORK MUST BE RE-OPENED EVEN
				// THOUGH INVENTORY HAS NOT TOUCHED IT.
				//
				// Unmapped waits on somebody stamping Inventory_Item_ID;
				// Blocked_Reduction waits on cloth coming back to Unallocated.
				// Neither changes last_modified_time, so the unchanged-document
				// shortcut below would skip them for ever and the line would sit
				// unapplied with the ledger cheerfully saying it had been seen.
				//----------------------------------------------------------
				lgStat = ifnull(lgRow.Sync_Status,"").toString().trim();

				if(lgStat == "Unmapped" || lgStat == "Blocked_Reduction")
				{
					if(!retryDocs.contains(lgDoc))
					{
						retryDocs.add(lgDoc);
					}
				}

				lgAppS = ifnull(lgRow.Applied_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
				if(lgAppS == "")
				{
					lgAppS = "0";
				}

				appliedByKey.put(lgKey,lgAppS.toDecimal());
				rowIdByKey.put(lgKey,lgRow.ID + "");
				modByDoc.put(lgDoc,ifnull(lgRow.Doc_Modified,"").toString().trim());

				lgList = keysByDoc.get(lgDoc);
				if(lgList == null)
				{
					lgList = List();
				}
				if(!lgList.contains(lgKey))
				{
					lgList.add(lgKey);
				}
				keysByDoc.put(lgDoc,lgList);
			}
		}

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// THE LIST. No date or sort parameter: a filter this org does not
		// accept fails the whole call, and a failed call reads exactly like an
		// endpoint that is not there. The window is applied in code instead,
		// and fullPage below says when pagination has become necessary.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		listUrl = baseUrl + "purchasereceives?organization_id=" + orgId + "&per_page=200";
		listKey = "purchasereceives";

		if(inflowSource == "Bill")
		{
			listUrl = baseUrl + "bills?organization_id=" + orgId + "&per_page=200";
			listKey = "bills";
		}

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// ZOHO HANDS DATES BACK AS yyyy-MM-dd AND DELUGE HERE READS dd-MMM-yyyy.
		//
		// Not a formatting preference - toDate() is parsed against the org's own
		// format, and the store widget already converts every date it sends into
		// dd-MMM-yyyy for exactly this reason (toDeluge, app/js/main.js). An ISO
		// string put through toDate() unconverted either throws or silently
		// resolves to the wrong day, and a wrong day here means an arrival falls
		// the wrong side of the cutover.
		//
		// Converted ONCE, in the list loop, and carried forward as dd-MMM-yyyy.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		monNames = {"Jan","Feb","Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug","Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec"};

		docIds = List();
		docNoByDoc = Map();
		docDateByDoc = Map();
		docModByDoc = Map();
		docLocByDoc = Map();

		callsUsed = callsUsed + 1;
		listResp = invokeurl
		[
			url :listUrl
			type :GET
			connection:"inventory_connection"
		];

		listCode = ifnull(listResp.get("code"),"-1").toString().trim();

		if(listCode != "0")
		{
			errTxt = listKey + " code " + listCode + ": " + ifnull(listResp.get("message"),"").toString();
		}
		else
		{
			listRows = ifnull(listResp.get(listKey),List());
			listedCount = listRows.size();

			if(listedCount >= 200)
			{
				listNote = "The list came back full at 200 rows - pagination is now needed and the oldest documents on this page may be missing.";
			}

			for each  dRow in listRows
			{
				dId = "";
				dNo = "";
				dDateTxt = "";
				dStatus = ifnull(dRow.get("status"),"").toString().trim().toLowerCase();

				// A receive carries BOTH, and they answer different questions:
				// status runs on to "billed" once the money side happens, so it
				// stops saying whether the cloth arrived. received_status is the
				// one that does. The probe's live receive read status "billed"
				// with received_status "received".
				dRcvStatus = ifnull(dRow.get("received_status"),"").toString().trim().toLowerCase();
				dLoc = ifnull(dRow.get("location_id"),"").toString().trim();
				dMod = ifnull(dRow.get("last_modified_time"),"").toString().trim();

				if(inflowSource == "Bill")
				{
					dId = ifnull(dRow.get("bill_id"),"").toString().trim();
					dNo = ifnull(dRow.get("bill_number"),"").toString().trim();
					dDateTxt = ifnull(dRow.get("date"),"").toString().trim();
				}
				else
				{
					dId = ifnull(dRow.get("purchasereceive_id"),"").toString().trim();
					dNo = ifnull(dRow.get("purchasereceive_number"),"").toString().trim();
					dDateTxt = ifnull(dRow.get("receive_date"),"").toString().trim();
				}

				keep = true;

				if(dId == "" || dDateTxt == "")
				{
					keep = false;
				}

				//----------------------------------------------------------
				// yyyy-MM-dd -> dd-MMM-yyyy. A timestamp field would carry a
				// time after the day, so only the first ten characters are
				// read; substring is valid lowercase in Deluge and both
				// spellings appear in this repo.
				//----------------------------------------------------------
				if(keep == true)
				{
					isoTxt = dDateTxt;
					if(isoTxt.length() > 10)
					{
						isoTxt = isoTxt.substring(0,10);
					}

					isoParts = isoTxt.toList("-");

					if(isoParts.size() != 3)
					{
						keep = false;
						if(noteJson != "")
						{
							noteJson = noteJson + ",";
						}
						noteJson = noteJson + "\"" + dNo.replaceAll("\"","'") + ": could not read the date '" + dDateTxt.replaceAll("\"","'") + "' - skipped\"";
					}
					else
					{
						monIdx = isoParts.get(1).toString().toNumber() - 1;

						if(monIdx < 0 || monIdx > 11)
						{
							keep = false;
						}
						else
						{
							dDateTxt = isoParts.get(2).toString() + "-" + monNames.get(monIdx) + "-" + isoParts.get(0).toString();
						}
					}
				}

				//----------------------------------------------------------
				// AN IN-TRANSIT RECEIVE HAS NOT MOVED STOCK. Zoho holds it
				// against the order until it is marked received; crediting it
				// would put cloth on the rack that is on a lorry - the same
				// distinction this app already makes between issue and receipt.
				//
				// A void or draft bill is the same case on the other branch.
				//----------------------------------------------------------
				if(keep == true && (dStatus == "in_transit" || dStatus == "draft" || dStatus == "void" || dStatus == "cancelled"))
				{
					keep = false;
					skippedDocs = skippedDocs + 1;
				}

				// Tested only when the field is actually present. Requiring it
				// outright would skip every document on a build of the API that
				// does not send it, which is the failure that looks like the
				// sync doing nothing at all.
				if(keep == true && dRcvStatus != "" && dRcvStatus != "received")
				{
					keep = false;
					skippedDocs = skippedDocs + 1;
				}

				if(keep == true)
				{
					// Relational operators work on dates - settled on the Deluge
					// tryout, and the same comparison createProductionPlans makes
					// on Plan_Start_Date.
					dDate = dDateTxt.toDate();

					if(dDate < cutoffDate)
					{
						keep = false;
					}
				}

				if(keep == true)
				{
					// Nothing changed since the ledger last read this document,
					// so it costs no call. This test is what keeps a run at one
					// call however long the purchase history gets.
					seenMod = ifnull(modByDoc.get(dId),"").toString();

					if(seenMod != "" && seenMod == dMod && !retryDocs.contains(dId))
					{
						keep = false;
						unchangedDocs = unchangedDocs + 1;
					}
				}

				if(keep == true)
				{
					if(docIds.size() >= maxDetail)
					{
						// No reliable break in a for each - counted and left for
						// the next run rather than pushed through this one.
						deferredDocs = deferredDocs + 1;
					}
					else
					{
						docIds.add(dId);
						docNoByDoc.put(dId,dNo);
						docDateByDoc.put(dId,dDateTxt);
						docModByDoc.put(dId,dMod);
						docLocByDoc.put(dId,dLoc);
					}
				}
			}
		}

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// The documents that have moved. One call each, and only these.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		for each  wDoc in docIds
		{
			if(errTxt == "")
			{
				detUrl = baseUrl + "purchasereceives/" + wDoc + "?organization_id=" + orgId;
				detKey = "purchasereceive";

				if(inflowSource == "Bill")
				{
					detUrl = baseUrl + "bills/" + wDoc + "?organization_id=" + orgId;
					detKey = "bill";
				}

				callsUsed = callsUsed + 1;
				detResp = invokeurl
				[
					url :detUrl
					type :GET
					connection:"inventory_connection"
				];

				if(ifnull(detResp.get("code"),"-1").toString().trim() != "0")
				{
					// Reported, not fatal. One unreadable document must not stop
					// the others landing, and it will be retried next run because
					// its ledger rows were never written.
					if(noteJson != "")
					{
						noteJson = noteJson + ",";
					}
					noteJson = noteJson + "\"" + ifnull(docNoByDoc.get(wDoc),wDoc).toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + ": detail call failed, left for the next run\"";
				}
				else
				{
					detBlock = detResp.get(detKey);

					if(detBlock != null)
					{
						detailCount = detailCount + 1;

						docNoTxt = ifnull(docNoByDoc.get(wDoc),"").toString();
						docDateTxt = ifnull(docDateByDoc.get(wDoc),"").toString();
						docModTxt = ifnull(docModByDoc.get(wDoc),"").toString();
						docLocTxt = ifnull(docLocByDoc.get(wDoc),"").toString();

						// The header carries the location on a receive; a bill
						// has none, so the line's warehouse is read instead
						// further down and this stays empty.
						if(docLocTxt == "")
						{
							docLocTxt = ifnull(detBlock.get("location_id"),"").toString().trim();
						}

						// No pre-cutover test here: cutoffDate is never earlier
						// than cutoverDate, so anything that reached this point
						// is already on the right side of it.
						docDate = docDateTxt.toDate();

						seenKeys = List();

						for each  dLine in ifnull(detBlock.get("line_items"),List())
						{
							lineId = ifnull(dLine.get("line_item_id"),"").toString().trim();
							invItem = ifnull(dLine.get("item_id"),"").toString().trim();

							lQtyS = ifnull(dLine.get("quantity"),"0").toString().trim();
							if(lQtyS == "")
							{
								lQtyS = "0";
							}
							docQty = lQtyS.toDecimal();

							lineKey = wDoc + "|" + lineId;
							seenKeys.add(lineKey);

							haveS = ifnull(appliedByKey.get(lineKey),"0").toString().trim();
							if(haveS == "")
							{
								haveS = "0";
							}
							haveQty = haveS.toDecimal();

							creatorMat = ifnull(matByInv.get(invItem),"").toString();
							isFabTxt = ifnull(fabByInv.get(invItem),"").toString();
							skuTxt = ifnull(skuByInv.get(invItem),"").toString();

							lineLoc = ifnull(dLine.get("warehouse_id"),"").toString().trim();
							if(lineLoc == "")
							{
								lineLoc = docLocTxt;
							}

							//==================================================
							// A PURCHASED ITEM CREATOR HAS NEVER HEARD OF.
							//
							// Without this the store is blocked on somebody
							// noticing an Unmapped ledger row and hand-building a
							// Raw_Material before any of that cloth can be given
							// a tone. Purchasing buys new materials routinely, so
							// that is the normal case, not the exception.
							//
							// It resolves in three ways, in this order, and only
							// the last one writes a new record:
							//
							//   1. A Raw_Material already carries this SKU but no
							//      Inventory_Item_ID. Stamp it and use it. This
							//      is the mapInventoryItemIds case arriving one
							//      material at a time, and creating a second row
							//      here would split one material in two - two
							//      SKUs, two stock balances, and every BOM
							//      pointing at the empty one.
							//   2. Inventory says it is not raw material. Refuse.
							//   3. Create it.
							//
							// ONE EXTRA CALL, ONCE PER NEW ITEM EVER. custom_fields
							// only comes back on the single-item read, and the
							// item is only read when the id is unknown.
							//==================================================
							//
							// Which way this line ends. Set BEFORE the auto-create
							// below, not after it - the auto-create writes lineNote
							// and can flip isFabTxt, and initialising afterwards
							// wiped both. targetTxt is therefore decided further
							// down, once isFabTxt is final.
							statusTxt = "Applied";
							targetTxt = "Quantity";
							wantDelta = docQty - haveQty;
							moveQty = wantDelta;
							lineNote = "";
							notRawItem = false;

							if(creatorMat == "" && autoCreate == true)
							{
								callsUsed = callsUsed + 1;

								itmResp = invokeurl
								[
									url :baseUrl + "items/" + invItem + "?organization_id=" + orgId
									type :GET
									connection:"inventory_connection"
								];

								if(ifnull(itmResp.get("code"),"-1").toString().trim() != "0")
								{
									lineNote = "Could not read Inventory item " + invItem + " to create it: " + ifnull(itmResp.get("message"),"").toString();
								}
								else
								{
									itmBlock = itmResp.get("item");

									if(itmBlock != null)
									{
										newSku = ifnull(itmBlock.get("sku"),"").toString().trim();
										newName = ifnull(itmBlock.get("name"),"").toString().trim();
										newUnit = ifnull(itmBlock.get("unit"),"").toString().trim();

										//------------------------------------------
										// READ BY customfield_id, NEVER BY LABEL.
										// Renaming the field in Inventory would
										// otherwise unclassify every item at once,
										// and the first symptom is purchases quietly
										// no longer landing. Settled as A3 in
										// inventory-integration.md.
										//------------------------------------------
										cvProduct = "";
										cvType = "";
										cvWidth = "";
										cvGsm = "";
										cvQuality = "";
										cvPattern = "";
										cvColor = "";

										for each  cfRow in ifnull(itmBlock.get("custom_fields"),List())
										{
											cfId = ifnull(cfRow.get("customfield_id"),"").toString().trim();
											cfVal = ifnull(cfRow.get("value"),"").toString().trim();

											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfProductType)
											{
												cvProduct = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfTypeField)
											{
												cvType = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfFabricWidth)
											{
												cvWidth = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfGsmField)
											{
												cvGsm = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfQualityField)
											{
												cvQuality = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfPatternField)
											{
												cvPattern = cfVal;
											}
											if(cfId != "" && cfId == cfColorField)
											{
												cvColor = cfVal;
											}
										}

										//------------------------------------------
										// 1. ALREADY IN CREATOR UNDER THIS SKU.
										//------------------------------------------
										bySku = "";
										bySkuFab = "no";

										if(newSku != "")
										{
											skuUp = newSku.toUpperCase();
											bySku = ifnull(unmappedIdBySku.get(skuUp),"").toString();
											bySkuFab = ifnull(unmappedFabBySku.get(skuUp),"no").toString();
										}

										// contains, not ==, and deliberately: the
										// Type field carries both "Fabric" and
										// "Printed fabric" and both ARE fabric. This
										// is not the stage-name case where substrings
										// collide - there are two values and one is
										// inside the other by design.
										isFabNew = false;

										if(cvType.toLowerCase().contains("fabric"))
										{
											isFabNew = true;
										}

										if(bySku != "")
										{
											if(writeAllowed == true)
											{
												for each  rmStamp in Raw_Material[ID == bySku.toLong()]
												{
													rmStamp.Inventory_Item_ID = invItem;
												}
											}

											creatorMat = bySku;
											skuTxt = newSku;
											isFabTxt = bySkuFab;
											matByInv.put(invItem,bySku);
											skuByInv.put(invItem,newSku);
											fabByInv.put(invItem,bySkuFab);

											// Off the unmapped index too, or a second
											// Inventory item with the same SKU would
											// be pointed at the same material.
											unmappedIdBySku.remove(newSku.toUpperCase());
											mappedNow = mappedNow + 1;
											lineNote = "Raw_Material " + newSku + " already existed and carried no Inventory_Item_ID - stamped it rather than creating a second material.";
										}
										else if(cfProductType == "")
										{
											lineNote = "Cannot classify Inventory item " + invItem + ": cfProductType is not set. Run probeItemCustomFields and put the customfield_id at the top of this function.";
										}
										else if(cvProduct == "")
										{
											lineNote = "Inventory item " + invItem + " (" + newSku + ") has no Product Type set, so there is nothing saying it is raw material. Set it in Inventory and this lands on the next run.";
										}
										else if(cvProduct.toLowerCase() != "raw material")
										{
											notRawItem = true;
											lineNote = "Inventory item " + invItem + " (" + newSku + ") is Product Type '" + cvProduct + "', not Raw Material. A finished good belongs to Item_Master, and creating it here would put it on the store's issue screen as cloth.";
										}
										else if(newSku == "")
										{
											lineNote = "Inventory item " + invItem + " has no SKU. SKU is the join key everywhere in this app and a Raw_Material without one cannot be found again - set it in Inventory and this lands on the next run.";
										}
										else if(newName == "")
										{
											lineNote = "Inventory item " + invItem + " has no name, and Name is mandatory on Raw_Material.";
										}
										else
										{
											//----------------------------------
											// 3. MINT IT. Same field list
											// sendToPrint uses, and Name is in
											// the block because it is MANDATORY -
											// setting it after the insert fails
											// the whole block with a message
											// reported thirty lines away.
											//
											// Every quantity starts at zero. The
											// arrival is applied by the ordinary
											// path below, so a material minted
											// here and one mapped by hand land
											// their stock through exactly the
											// same code.
											//----------------------------------
											wNew = 0.0;

											if(cvWidth != "")
											{
												wNew = cvWidth.toDecimal();
											}

											gNew = 0.0;

											if(cvGsm != "")
											{
												gNew = cvGsm.toDecimal();
											}

											// A DRY RUN LEAVES creatorMat AS "0", not as
											// a made-up id. Raw_Material[ID == 0]
											// matches nothing, so the reads below
											// find zero on hand and no write is
											// attempted - where a placeholder string
											// would throw on .toLong() and take the
											// whole run down.
											if(writeAllowed == true)
											{
												newMatId = insert into Raw_Material
												[
													Name=newName
													Material_Display_Name=newName
													SKU=newSku
													Is_Fabric=isFabNew
													Type_field=cvType
													Pattern=cvPattern
													Color=cvColor
													Quality=cvQuality
													Unit=newUnit
													Fabric_Width_Inches=wNew
													Fabric_Gsm=gNew
													Inventory_Item_ID=invItem
													Quantity=0
													Wash_Quantity=0
													Unwash_Quantity=0
													In_Wash_Qty=0
													In_Print_Qty=0
													In_Transit_Qty=0
													Disputed_Qty=0
													Unallocated_Qty=0
													Added_User=zoho.loginuser
												];

												creatorMat = newMatId.toString();
											}
											else
											{
												creatorMat = "0";
											}

											skuTxt = newSku;
											createdMats = createdMats + 1;

											if(isFabNew == true)
											{
												isFabTxt = "yes";
											}
											else
											{
												isFabTxt = "no";
											}

											if(writeAllowed == true)
											{
												matByInv.put(invItem,creatorMat);
												skuByInv.put(invItem,newSku);
												fabByInv.put(invItem,isFabTxt);
											}

											lineNote = "Raw_Material " + newSku + " created automatically from Inventory.";

											//----------------------------------
											// A FABRIC WITH NO WIDTH IS NOT A
											// REASON TO REFUSE THE CLOTH - it is
											// really on the rack and saying so is
											// right. But the cut maths divides by
											// the width, so it has to be filled in
											// before this material can be planned.
											// Said here and in the run report,
											// because nothing downstream will.
											//----------------------------------
											if(isFabNew == true && wNew <= 0)
											{
												lineNote = lineNote + " NO FABRIC WIDTH - the cut calculation needs Fabric_Width_Inches and this material cannot be planned until it is set by hand.";
												widthMissing = widthMissing + 1;

												if(noteJson != "")
												{
													noteJson = noteJson + ",";
												}
												noteJson = noteJson + "\"" + newSku.replaceAll("\"","'") + " was created as fabric with NO width - set Fabric_Width_Inches before it is used in a BOM\"";
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}

							//--------------------------------------------------
							// A BILL LINE THAT NAMES A RECEIVE HAS ALREADY MOVED
							// STOCK. It can only appear when inflowSource says
							// Bill while the org is in fact using receives -
							// i.e. the setting changed underneath this constant.
							// Applying it would double every arrival, so it is
							// refused and named rather than trusted.
							//--------------------------------------------------
							dupRcv = ifnull(dLine.get("receive_item_id"),"").toString().trim();

							if(isFabTxt == "yes")
							{
								targetTxt = "Unallocated";
							}

							if(creatorMat == "" && notRawItem == true)
							{
								//------------------------------------------
								// NOT RAW MATERIAL, AND NEVER RETRIED.
								// Unmapped re-opens its document every run
								// because it is waiting on somebody. This is
								// not waiting on anybody - Inventory has
								// answered, and the answer is that this is not
								// the store's cloth. Retrying it would open the
								// document and read the item for ever.
								//------------------------------------------
								statusTxt = "Skipped_Not_Raw_Material";
								moveQty = 0;
								notRawLines = notRawLines + 1;
							}
							else if(creatorMat == "")
							{
								statusTxt = "Unmapped";
								moveQty = 0;

								// Whatever the auto-create found is far more use
								// than the generic line, so it is only used when
								// nothing else was said.
								if(lineNote == "")
								{
									lineNote = "No Raw_Material carries Inventory_Item_ID " + invItem + " - map it and this lands on the next run.";
								}

								unmappedLines = unmappedLines + 1;
							}
							else if(inflowSource == "Bill" && dupRcv != "")
							{
								statusTxt = "Skipped_Duplicate";
								moveQty = 0;
								lineNote = "This bill line came from purchase receive item " + dupRcv + ", which already moved the stock. inflowSource says Bill but this org is using receives - check probePurchaseInflow again.";
								skippedLines = skippedLines + 1;
							}

							//--------------------------------------------------
							// A REDUCTION STOPS AT ZERO AND NEVER TOUCHES A LOT.
							//
							// Once the store person has given cloth a tone it is
							// in a lot, and which lot loses metres when a receive
							// is corrected downwards is a decision only he can
							// make - he can see the rack. Taking it off a lot
							// here would be the system choosing a tone, which is
							// the one thing lots exist to prevent.
							//
							// So the reduction takes what Unallocated_Qty still
							// holds and the remainder is recorded at
							// Blocked_Reduction for a person to settle. The
							// ledger keeps the unapplied part, so nothing is
							// quietly forgotten and reconcileRawMaterial will
							// name the SKU.
							//--------------------------------------------------
							haveNow = 0.0;

							if(statusTxt == "Applied" && moveQty != 0)
							{
								for each  rmRead in Raw_Material[ID == creatorMat.toLong()]
								{
									if(targetTxt == "Unallocated")
									{
										rdS = ifnull(rmRead.Unallocated_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
									}
									else
									{
										rdS = ifnull(rmRead.Quantity,"0").toString().trim();
									}
									if(rdS == "")
									{
										rdS = "0";
									}
									haveNow = rdS.toDecimal();
								}

								if(moveQty < 0 && (haveNow + moveQty) < 0)
								{
									shortfallQty = 0 - (haveNow + moveQty);
									moveQty = 0 - haveNow;
									statusTxt = "Blocked_Reduction";

									whereGone = "has already been put into lots and must be taken off one by hand";
									if(targetTxt == "Quantity")
									{
										whereGone = "has already been issued or consumed and must be corrected by hand";
									}

									lineNote = "Corrected downwards by " + (0 - wantDelta) + " but only " + haveNow + " was still available to take back. " + shortfallQty + " " + whereGone + ".";
									blockedLines = blockedLines + 1;
								}
							}

							if(writeAllowed == true && statusTxt != "Unmapped" && moveQty != 0)
							{
								for each  rmUpd in Raw_Material[ID == creatorMat.toLong()]
								{
									if(targetTxt == "Unallocated")
									{
										uwS = ifnull(rmUpd.Unallocated_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
										if(uwS == "")
										{
											uwS = "0";
										}
										rmUpd.Unallocated_Qty = uwS.toDecimal() + moveQty;
									}
									else
									{
										qwS = ifnull(rmUpd.Quantity,"0").toString().trim();
										if(qwS == "")
										{
											qwS = "0";
										}
										rmUpd.Quantity = qwS.toDecimal() + moveQty;
									}
								}
							}

							if(moveQty != 0)
							{
								appliedLines = appliedLines + 1;

								if(targetTxt == "Unallocated")
								{
									netFabric = netFabric + moveQty;
								}
								else
								{
									netOther = netOther + moveQty;
								}
							}

							newApplied = haveQty + moveQty;

							if(writeAllowed == true)
							{
								existRow = ifnull(rowIdByKey.get(lineKey),"").toString();

								if(existRow != "")
								{
									for each  lgUpd in Inventory_Inflow[ID == existRow.toLong()]
									{
										lgUpd.Doc_Qty = docQty;
										lgUpd.Applied_Qty = newApplied;
										lgUpd.Doc_Modified = docModTxt;
										lgUpd.Sync_Status = statusTxt;
										lgUpd.Note = lineNote;
									}
								}
								else
								{
									// No comment may appear inside this field list -
									// the block is parsed specially and a // line in
									// it is a syntax error reported against the
									// function's opening try, thousands of lines away.
									newLg = insert into Inventory_Inflow
									[
										Doc_Type=inflowSource
										Doc_ID=wDoc
										Doc_No=docNoTxt
										Doc_Date=docDate
										Doc_Modified=docModTxt
										Line_ID=lineId
										Inventory_Item_ID=invItem
										Doc_Qty=docQty
										Applied_Qty=newApplied
										Target=targetTxt
										Location_ID=lineLoc
										Sync_Status=statusTxt
										Note=lineNote
										Added_User=zoho.loginuser
									];

									// The lookup goes on after the insert - a null
									// cannot go into the block, and an unmapped line
									// legitimately has no material behind it.
									if(creatorMat != "")
									{
										for each  lgNew in Inventory_Inflow[ID == newLg.toLong()]
										{
											lgNew.Material = creatorMat.toLong();
										}
									}
								}
							}

							if(rowsJson != "")
							{
								rowsJson = rowsJson + ",";
							}

							// Free text through the whole chain, not just the
							// quote. A raw newline inside a JSON string literal is
							// invalid JSON and Deluge does not throw on it - the
							// widget gets "bad control character" and nothing
							// renders.
							rowsJson = rowsJson + "{\"doc\":\"" + docNoTxt.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"date\":\"" + docDateTxt + "\",\"sku\":\"" + skuTxt.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"itemId\":\"" + invItem + "\",\"target\":\"" + targetTxt + "\",\"docQty\":" + docQty + ",\"alreadyApplied\":" + haveQty + ",\"applying\":" + moveQty + ",\"status\":\"" + statusTxt + "\",\"note\":\"" + lineNote.replaceAll("\"","'").replaceAll("\r","").replaceAll("\n"," | ").replaceAll("\t"," ") + "\"}";
						}

						//------------------------------------------------------
						// A LINE THE DOCUMENT NO LONGER HAS. Deleting a line off
						// a receive is a correction like any other, and the only
						// place it exists is as a ledger key with nothing
						// matching it. Reversed by exactly what it took in.
						//------------------------------------------------------
						oldKeys = keysByDoc.get(wDoc);

						if(oldKeys != null)
						{
							for each  oldKey in oldKeys
							{
								gonRow = ifnull(rowIdByKey.get(oldKey),"").toString().trim();

								// Guarded on the row id as well as the key. An
								// empty id makes .toLong() throw "Error while
								// fetching record", which says nothing about the
								// real problem.
								if(!seenKeys.contains(oldKey) && gonRow != "")
								{
									backS = ifnull(appliedByKey.get(oldKey),"0").toString().trim();
									if(backS == "")
									{
										backS = "0";
									}
									backQty = backS.toDecimal();

									gonMat = "";
									gonTarget = "Quantity";

									for each  gonRead in Inventory_Inflow[ID == gonRow.toLong()]
									{
										gonMat = ifnull(gonRead.Material,"").toString().trim();

										// ifnull does not catch EMPTY, and a
										// Target read as "" would send a fabric
										// reversal at Quantity, which nothing
										// reads and which leaves Unallocated_Qty
										// overstated for ever.
										gonTgtTxt = ifnull(gonRead.Target,"").toString().trim();
										if(gonTgtTxt != "")
										{
											gonTarget = gonTgtTxt;
										}
									}

									gonMove = 0.0;

									if(backQty > 0 && gonMat != "")
									{
										gonHave = 0.0;

										for each  gonMatRead in Raw_Material[ID == gonMat.toLong()]
										{
											if(gonTarget == "Unallocated")
											{
												ghS = ifnull(gonMatRead.Unallocated_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
											}
											else
											{
												ghS = ifnull(gonMatRead.Quantity,"0").toString().trim();
											}
											if(ghS == "")
											{
												ghS = "0";
											}
											gonHave = ghS.toDecimal();
										}

										gonMove = backQty;
										if(gonMove > gonHave)
										{
											gonMove = gonHave;
										}

										if(writeAllowed == true && gonMove > 0)
										{
											for each  gonUpd in Raw_Material[ID == gonMat.toLong()]
											{
												if(gonTarget == "Unallocated")
												{
													guS = ifnull(gonUpd.Unallocated_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
													if(guS == "")
													{
														guS = "0";
													}
													gonUpd.Unallocated_Qty = guS.toDecimal() - gonMove;
												}
												else
												{
													gqS = ifnull(gonUpd.Quantity,"0").toString().trim();
													if(gqS == "")
													{
														gqS = "0";
													}
													gonUpd.Quantity = gqS.toDecimal() - gonMove;
												}
											}
										}
									}

									gonStatus = "Applied";
									gonNote = "The line was removed from " + ifnull(docNoByDoc.get(wDoc),wDoc).toString() + " - what it had taken in was reversed.";

									if(gonMove < backQty)
									{
										gonStatus = "Blocked_Reduction";
										gonNote = "The line was removed from " + ifnull(docNoByDoc.get(wDoc),wDoc).toString() + " but only " + gonMove + " of " + backQty + " was still unallocated. The rest is in lots and must be taken off one by hand.";
										blockedLines = blockedLines + 1;
									}

									if(writeAllowed == true)
									{
										for each  gonWrite in Inventory_Inflow[ID == gonRow.toLong()]
										{
											gonWrite.Doc_Qty = 0;
											gonWrite.Applied_Qty = backQty - gonMove;
											gonWrite.Doc_Modified = ifnull(docModByDoc.get(wDoc),"").toString();
											gonWrite.Sync_Status = gonStatus;
											gonWrite.Note = gonNote;
										}
									}

									if(gonMove > 0)
									{
										reversedLines = reversedLines + 1;

										if(gonTarget == "Unallocated")
										{
											netFabric = netFabric - gonMove;
										}
										else
										{
											netOther = netOther - gonMove;
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}

		if(listNote != "")
		{
			if(noteJson != "")
			{
				noteJson = noteJson + ",";
			}
			noteJson = noteJson + "\"" + listNote + "\"";
		}

		errJson = "";
		if(errTxt != "")
		{
			errJson = "\"" + errTxt.replaceAll("\"","'").replaceAll("\r","").replaceAll("\n"," | ") + "\"";
		}

		info "syncPurchaseInflow | dryRun=" + dryTxtOut + " source=" + inflowSource + " listed=" + listedCount + " opened=" + detailCount + " appliedLines=" + appliedLines + " reversed=" + reversedLines + " unmapped=" + unmappedLines + " blocked=" + blockedLines + " created=" + createdMats + " stamped=" + mappedNow + " notRaw=" + notRawLines + " noWidth=" + widthMissing + " calls=" + callsUsed;

		// Built by hand - Map.toString() does not emit valid JSON once the
		// structure nests, and List.toString() does not wrap in [].
		res = "{\"errors\":[" + errJson + "],\"dryRun\":" + dryTxtOut + ",\"source\":\"" + inflowSource + "\",\"callsUsed\":" + callsUsed + ",\"listed\":" + listedCount + ",\"opened\":" + detailCount + ",\"unchanged\":" + unchangedDocs + ",\"skippedDocs\":" + skippedDocs + ",\"skippedLines\":" + skippedLines + ",\"deferred\":" + deferredDocs + ",\"appliedLines\":" + appliedLines + ",\"reversedLines\":" + reversedLines + ",\"unmappedLines\":" + unmappedLines + ",\"blockedLines\":" + blockedLines + ",\"materialsCreated\":" + createdMats + ",\"materialsStamped\":" + mappedNow + ",\"notRawMaterialLines\":" + notRawLines + ",\"createdWithoutWidth\":" + widthMissing + ",\"netToUnallocated\":" + netFabric + ",\"netToQuantity\":" + netOther + ",\"notes\":[" + noteJson + "],\"lines\":[" + rowsJson + "]}";
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		// Creator reports every runtime failure as a generic code 9430, so the
		// real message has to travel back inside the payload.
		errTxt = "DELUGE: " + e.toString();
	}

	// ONE EXIT, AT THE BOTTOM. Deluge's "all paths return" check does not count
	// a return that lives inside try/catch, and a function whose every return
	// sits in the try fails to save with "Missing return statement" reported
	// against the first line of the body. Same shape as issueMaterials.
	if(res == "")
	{
		if(errTxt == "")
		{
			errTxt = "Nothing ran";
		}
		res = "{\"errors\":[\"" + errTxt.replaceAll("\"","'").replaceAll("\r","").replaceAll("\n"," | ") + "\"]}";
	}

	return res;
}
